            <div class='titles'>360AI — Privacy Policy</div><br>
			<div class='paragraphs'>
			<div class='paragraphs'>
				<b>1. Overview</b><br><br>

				This Privacy Policy explains how 360AI collects, uses, stores, and protects your information. By using 360AI, you consent to the practices described here.<br><br>

				<b>2. Information We Collect</b><br><br>

				<b>a. Account Information</b><br><br>

					Email address<br><br>

					Membership number<br><br>

					Password (stored securely)<br><br>

				<b>b. Session Information</b><br><br>

					Session ID<br><br>

					IP address<br><br>

					User agent<br><br>

					Login timestamps<br><br>

				<b>c. Interaction Data</b><br><br>

					360AI may store reinforcement signals (approve/deny), message logs, and system behavior metrics to improve clarity, stability, and user experience.<br><br>

					Important: Individual words, sentences, or paragraphs entered into the AI cannot be selectively deleted once processed. They may exist in logs or system behavior records.<br><br>

				<b>3. How We Use Your Information</b><br><br>

					Authenticate your account<br><br>

					Maintain secure sessions<br><br>

					Improve AI clarity and stability<br><br>

					Provide personalized system behavior<br><br>

					Prevent abuse or misuse<br><br>

					Maintain platform integrity<br><br>

				<b>4. Cookies</b><br><br>

					360AI uses cookies to:<br><br>

					Keep you logged in<br><br>

					Maintain session continuity<br><br>

					Enhance security<br><br>

					You may disable cookies, but some features will not function.<br><br>

				<b>5. Data Storage & Retention</b><br><br>

				<b>a. Account Data</b><br><br>

					Stored until the user requests deletion.<br><br>

				<b>b. Chat Group Saves</b><br><br>

					Users may delete chat-group saves. Once deleted, they are removed from the database.<br><br>

				<b>c. AI Input Data</b><br><br>

					Words, sentences, and paragraphs entered into the AI cannot be individually removed. This includes message logs, reinforcement signals, and system behavior metrics. These records may persist as part of system operation.<br><br>

				<b>d. Session Data</b><br><br>

					Session entries are removed upon logout or expiration.<br><br>

				<b>6. Data Sharing</b><br><br>

					360AI does not sell, rent, or share your personal information with third parties. Data may be disclosed only if required by law or to protect system integrity.<br><br>

				<b>7. User Control</b><br><br>

					You may request:<br><br>

					Account deletion<br><br>

					Correction of personal information<br><br>

					Removal of chat-group saves<br><br>

					You cannot request deletion of individual AI inputs, message fragments, or specific conversation lines.<br><br>

					Upon account deletion, account data, associated chat-group saves, and session data are removed. AI input logs are not individually purged.<br><br>

				<b>8. Security</b><br><br>

					360AI uses secure session identifiers, signed cookies, and controlled database access to protect your information. While no system is perfectly secure, reasonable measures are taken to safeguard data.<br><br>

				<b>9. Children’s Privacy</b><br><br>

					360AI is not intended for users under 18.<br><br>

				<b>10. Changes to Policy</b><br><br>

					This Privacy Policy may be updated. Continued use of 360AI indicates acceptance of any changes.<br><br>

				<b>11. Contact</b><br><br>

					For privacy questions, contact the 360AI administrator.<br><br>
